# Claude agent files.
#
# Most of this directory is per-machine state, but three things in it are PROJECT TOOLING and
# have to travel with the repo: the shared settings (which wire up the PostToolUse edit guard),
# the hook scripts themselves, and the skills. Ignoring them wholesale meant they existed only on
# the machine that wrote them - invisible to a fresh clone, to the CachyOS install, and to any
# `git worktree` (which does not copy ignored files at all). CLAUDE.md already cites
# `.claude/skills/gitnexus/*/SKILL.md` by path, and those citations pointed at nothing for anyone
# who had not generated them locally.
#
# Note on the syntax: git does not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so `!` on a file inside an
# ignored directory has no effect. Excluding the children with `/*` and then re-including the
# specific subdirectories is what makes the negations work.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/settings.json
!/.claude/scripts/
!/.claude/skills/
